cauchyMap -- produces one surjection from the Cauchy decomposition of the exterior power of a tensor product
************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        cauchyMap(b,E)
  * Inputs:
      * b, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * E, a *note free module with labeled basis: LabeledModule,, must be a
        tensor product
  * Outputs:
      * a *note map of labeled modules: LabeledModuleMap,, 

Description
===========

We begin with a module $E$ that was constructed as a tensor product $E=A\otimes
B$, where $A$ and $B$ are free modules. Cauchy decomposition provides a formula
for decomposing $\wedge^b E$ as $GL(A)\times GL(B)$ representations.  This
function constructs the surjection onto the $\wedge^b A\otimes S^b B$ factor:
$$ \wedge^b E \to \wedge^b A\otimes S^b B. $$

