flattenedESTensor -- make a flattened tensor from elementary symmetric functions
********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        flattenedESTensor(L,kk)
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of positive ZZ
      * kk, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, Name of ground field (or ring)
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * MonSize (missing documentation) => ..., default value 32, 
  * Outputs:
      * f, a *note map of labeled modules: LabeledModuleMap,, 

Description
===========

Given a list $L = \{a, b_1,\dots, b_n\}$ of positive integers with $ a= sum_i
b_i, $ and a field (or ring of integers) kk, the script creates a ring $S =
kk[x_1,\dots,x_n]$ and a map $$ f: A \to B_1\otimes\cdots \otimes B_n $$ of
*note LabeledModule: LabeledModule,s over $S$, where $A$ is a free
LabeledModule of rank $a$ and $B_i$ is a free LabeledModule of rank $b_i$. The
map $f$ is constructed from symmetric functions, and corresponds to collection
of linear forms on $P^{b_1-1}\times\cdots\timesß P^{b_n-1}$ as used in the
construction of pure resolutions in the paper ``Betti numbers of graded modules
and cohomology of vector bundles'' of Eisenbud and Schreyer.

The format of $F$ is the one required by *note tensorComplex1: tensorComplex1,,
namely $f: A \to B_1\otimes \cdots \otimes B_n$, with $a = rank A, b_i = rank
B_i$.

There is an OPTION, MonSize => n (where n is 8,16, or 32). This sets the *note
MonomialSize: (Macaulay2Doc)MonomialSize, option when the base ring of
flattenedESTensor is created.



