LabeledModule -- the class of free modules with a labeled basis
***************************************************************

Description
===========

A labeled module $F$ is a free module together with two additional pieces of
data: a *note basisList: basisList, which corresponds to the basis of $F$, and
a list of *note underlyingModules: underlyingModules, which were used in the
construction of $F$. The constructor *note labeledModule: labeledModule, can be
used to construct a labeled module from a free module. The call labeledModule
E, where $E$ is a free module, returns a labeled module with *note basisList:
basisList, $\{1,\dots, rank E\}$ and *note underlyingModules:
underlyingModules, $\{E\}$.ß

For example if $A,B$ are of type LabeledModule, then F=tensorProduct(A,B)
constructs the LabeledModule $F=A\otimes B$ with *note basisList: basisList,
equal to the list of pairs $\{a,b\}$ where $a$ belongs to the basis list of $A$
and $b$ belongs to the basis list of $b$. The list of *note underlyingModules:
underlyingModules, of $F$ is $\{A,B\}$.

Certain functors which are the identity in the category of modules are
non-trivial isomorphisms in the category of labeled modules.  For example, if F
is a labeled module with basis list \{0,1\} then tensorProduct F is a labeled
free module with basis list \{\{ 0\},\{ 1\}\} .  Similarly, one must be careful
when applying the functors *note exteriorPower: (Macaulay2Doc)exteriorPower,
and *note symmetricPower: (Macaulay2Doc)symmetricPower,.  For a ring $S$, the
multiplicative unit for tensor product is the rank 1 free $S$-module whose
generator is labeled by \{\} . This is constructed by labeledModule S.

Functions and methods returning a free module with labeled basis:
=================================================================

  * *note labeledModule: labeledModule, -- makes a labeled module
  * *note tensor(LabeledModule,LabeledModule):
    tensor_lpLabeledModule_cmLabeledModule_rp, -- creates the tensor product of
    two labeled modules, as a labeled module

