labeledModule -- makes a labeled module
***************************************

  * Usage: 
        labeledModule M
        labeledModule R
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, which is free
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note free module with labeled basis: LabeledModule,, 

Description
===========

This is the basic construction for a *note LabeledModule: LabeledModule,.
Given a free module $M$ of rank $r$, this constructs a labeled module with
basis labeled by $\{0,..,r-1\}$ and no underlying modules.

+-------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/101[a,b,c];              |
+-------------------------------------+
|i2 : E = labeledModule S^3           |
|                                     |
|      3                              |
|o2 = S                               |
|                                     |
|o2 : free S-module with labeled basis|
+-------------------------------------+
|i3 : basisList E                     |
|                                     |
|o3 = {0, 1, 2}                       |
|                                     |
|o3 : List                            |
+-------------------------------------+
|i4 : underlyingModules E             |
|                                     |
|o4 = {}                              |
|                                     |
|o4 : List                            |
+-------------------------------------+
|i5 : module E                        |
|                                     |
|      3                              |
|o5 = S                               |
|                                     |
|o5 : S-module, free                  |
+-------------------------------------+
|i6 : rank E                          |
|                                     |
|o6 = 3                               |
+-------------------------------------+

For technical reasons, it is often convenient to construct a rank $1$ free
module whose generator is labeled by the empty set. This is constructed by
labeledModule S.





+--------------------------------------+
|i7 : S = ZZ/101[a,b,c];               |
+--------------------------------------+
|i8 : F = labeledModule S              |
|                                      |
|      1                               |
|o8 = S                                |
|                                      |
|o8 : free S-module with labeled basis |
+--------------------------------------+
|i9 : basisList F                      |
|                                      |
|o9 = {{}}                             |
|                                      |
|o9 : List                             |
+--------------------------------------+
|i10 : underlyingModules F             |
|                                      |
|o10 = {}                              |
|                                      |
|o10 : List                            |
+--------------------------------------+
|i11 : module F                        |
|                                      |
|       1                              |
|o11 = S                               |
|                                      |
|o11 : S-module, free                  |
+--------------------------------------+
|i12 : E = labeledModule S^1           |
|                                      |
|       1                              |
|o12 = S                               |
|                                      |
|o12 : free S-module with labeled basis|
+--------------------------------------+
|i13 : basisList E                     |
|                                      |
|o13 = {0}                             |
|                                      |
|o13 : List                            |
+--------------------------------------+
|i14 : underlyingModules E             |
|                                      |
|o14 = {}                              |
|                                      |
|o14 : List                            |
+--------------------------------------+

