toOrdinal -- turns the label of a basis element of a labeled module into a corresponding ordinal
************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        toOrdinal(i,F)
  * Inputs:
      * l, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, 
      * F, a *note free module with labeled basis: LabeledModule,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 

Description
===========

This function allows one to move from the labels of the basis elements of a
labeled free module of rank $r$ to the integers $\{0,1, \dots, r-1\}$. More
specifically, if $F$ is a labeled free module where we have labeled the basis
with the list $L$, then this function an element  $l\in L$ to the ordinal $j$
such that $l$ is the $j$'th element of $L$.



+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S=ZZ/101[x_{0,0,0}..x_{2,1,1}];                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
