underlyingModules -- gives the list of underlying modules of a labeled module
*****************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        underlyingModules(F)
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note free module with labeled basis: LabeledModule,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

One of the key features of a labeled module is that it comes equipped with a
list of modules used in its construction.  For instance, if $F$ is the tensor
product of $A$ and $B$, then the underlying modules of $F$ would be the set $\{
A,B\}$.  Similarly, if $G=\wedge^2 A$, then $A$ is the only underlying module
of $G$.



+-------------------------------------+
|i1 : S=ZZ/101[x,y,z];                |
+-------------------------------------+
|i2 : A=labeledModule(S^2);           |
|                                     |
|o2 : free S-module with labeled basis|
+-------------------------------------+
|i3 : B=labeledModule(S^5);           |
|                                     |
|o3 : free S-module with labeled basis|
+-------------------------------------+
|i4 : F=A**B                          |
|                                     |
|      10                             |
|o4 = S                               |
|                                     |
|o4 : free S-module with labeled basis|
+-------------------------------------+
|i5 : underlyingModules(F)            |
|                                     |
|       2   5                         |
|o5 = {S , S }                        |
|                                     |
|o5 : List                            |
+-------------------------------------+
|i6 : G=exteriorPower(2,A)            |
|                                     |
|      1                              |
|o6 = S                               |
|                                     |
|o6 : free S-module with labeled basis|
+-------------------------------------+
|i7 : underlyingModules(G)            |
|                                     |
|       2                             |
|o7 = {S }                            |
|                                     |
|o7 : List                            |
+-------------------------------------+

